Synology DSM / NAS MIBs

Source: Synology SNMP MIB Guide, "Supported MIB files":
https://kb.synology.com/en-us/DG/Synology_DiskStation_MIB_Guide/2

Official archive (downloaded 2026-10-02):
https://global.download.synology.com/download/Document/Software/DeveloperGuide/Firmware/SynologyOS/All/enu/Synology_MIB_File.zip
SHA256: 6514007468a577a3483e35c03280e0c36dc269658f4270756507073c646fe781

Import the complete 21-module vendor bundle together. It covers DSM system,
disk, RAID, SMART, UPS, storage I/O, iSCSI, NFS, SMB and MailPlus monitoring,
and also includes modules for DSM Enterprise, SRM and ActiveProtect Manager.
Availability of individual objects depends on the device and installed OS.
The older Firmware/DSM archive contains only 16 modules; use the SynologyOS
archive linked by the current guide for future updates.

Prepared with EXTRAS/scripts/prepmibs: filenames normalized to .mib and
line endings to LF. Module names and OID definitions are preserved.
Validated with EXTRAS/scripts/testload synology and EXTRAS/scripts/genxlate
using Net-SNMP 5.9.4 in the EXTRAS/contrib/Dockerfile toolset with
Alpine 3.21. The MIBs also pass testload with Net-SNMP 5.9.5.2.
